Any updates on this? We finally got #40062 solved (but not merged with 26), and now this is blocking us from upgrading to 27 😭. We're stuck on 25 with a horrible bug where sharing screen during a call will crash the full app randomly.

@participant18 let us know if there's any way we can support you in testing or being guinea pigs. cc. @participant32 

Much gratitude, as always, for supporting this project 🙏

As a workaround, set the background as `#00000000` when the window is foucsed or blurred can hide the title bar

```javascript
win.on('blur', () => {
  win.setBackgroundColor('#00000000')
})

win.on('focus', () => {
  win.setBackgroundColor('#00000000')
})
```

```javascript
/**/
function createWindow() {
	win = new BrowserWindow({
		width: 1600,
		height: 900,
		frame: false,
		transparent: true,
		backgroundColor: "#00000000",
	});

	win.loadFile("index.html");

	/* Electron issues 39959 */
	/* Electron27.0.3 On win11, Electron 28.0.0 on Win10 22H2 X64*/
	/* Temporary solution: Modify window size when the window is focused or blurred */
	/* (Whether modifying the height or the width, the page content may shake, please choose according to your needs) */
	
	/* Using Electron26.6.2 may not have this issue. For me, this bug may not appear.*/
	/* Electron26.6.2 cannot click through the transparent area */
	/* Electron27.0.3 and 28.0.0 can click through the transparent area */
	
	if (/^(27|28)\.\d+\.\d+(\-alpha\.\d+|\-beta\.\d+)?$/.test(process.versions.electron) && process.platform === "win32") {
		win.on("blur", () => {
			const[width_39959, height_39959] = win.getSize();
			win.setSize(width_39959, height_39959 + 1);
			win.setSize(width_39959, height_39959);
		});
		win.on("focus", () => {
			const[width_39959, height_39959] = win.getSize();
			win.setSize(width_39959, height_39959 + 1);
			win.setSize(width_39959, height_39959);
		});
	}
}
/**/
```

