Can confirm the problem exists in v32 as well as there's a problem with this solution as well. the height restore part doesn't work. Tried even with a timeout. and as the window keep loosing focus and get into focus, it keeps growing. I solved that problem using `win.setResizeable()` like this:

```
         win.on("blur", () => {
		setupWindow.setResizable(true);
		const [w, h] = setupWindow.getSize();
		setupWindow.setSize(w, h + 1);
		setupWindow.setSize(w, h);
		setupWindow.setResizable(false);
	});
	win.on("focus", () => {
		setupWindow.setResizable(true);
		const [w, h] = setupWindow.getSize();
		setupWindow.setSize(w, h + 1);
		setupWindow.setSize(w, h);
		setupWindow.setResizable(false);
	});
```

I have a version that doesn't flash. You essentially stop rendering, do the flash, then re-enable flash. 

This is what I have, roughly:

```
const runWorkaround = () => {
	if( yourWindow && !yourWindow.isDestroyed()) {
		// Pause rendering
		yourWindow.webContents.setFrameRate(0)
		const [width, height] = yourWindow.getSize()
		yourWindow.setSize(width, height + 1)
		process.nextTick(() => {
			if( yourWindow && !yourWindow.isDestroyed()) {
				trayWindow.setSize(width, height)
				trayWindow.webContents.setFrameRate(60)
			}
		})
	}
}

yourWindow.webContents.on('before-input-event', runWorkaround)
yourWindow.webContents.on('focus', runWorkaround)
yourWindow.webContents.on('blur', runWorkaround)
```

Thank you @participant21 for your workaround. I could not have created this one without yours.
